<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Did anyone notice in  the interview whith Charlie Otero that he mentions his mother is a hypnotist? <BR> &#34;And she would do her best to help other people.  She was known to help people with psychotic problems.  Like uh, she would hypnotize.  I’ve seen her hypnotize people into not stuttering who have stuttered all their lives.  And I’ve seen her calm people down who were hysterical over things that have happened.&#34; <BR>I&#39;m wondering if Charlie can remember anyone who was hypnotized by his mother,then again this sounds like more info withheld by wpd.Anybody?  <BR> <BR>Here is the link to the interview: <BR><a href="http://www.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite?pagename=KWCH%2FMGArticle%2FWCH_BasicArticle&amp;c=MGArticle&amp;cid=1031776799370&amp;path=" target=_top>http://www.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite?pagename=KWC H%2FMGArticle%2FWCH_BasicArticle&amp;c=MGArticle&amp;cid=1 031776799370&amp;path=</a>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5471-->
